          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Square Pairs!"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.166,
            0.632,
            0.183
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Look at the following numbers: 3 6 10 15 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.185,
            0.847,
            0.222
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "They are arranged such that each pair of adjacent numbers adds up to a square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.282,
            0.226,
            0.716,
            0.245
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_17_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "3+6=9,6+10=16,10+15=25,15+1=16."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.251,
            0.848,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try arranging the numbers 1 to 17 (without repetition) in a row in a similar way — the sum of every adjacent pair of numbers should be a square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.306,
            0.847,
            0.344
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you arrange them in more than one way? If not, can you explain why?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.38,
            0.847,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you do the same with numbers from 1 to 32 (again, without repetition), but this time arranging all the numbers in a circle?"
            }
          ]
        },
